  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Launchpad for African SMEs to access Global markets</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project proposes to support 3000 Small and Medium Enterprises in Kenya, Ethiopia, Uganda, Tanzania, Rwanda and Ghana with a comprehensive package of digital tools and expertise (Digital LaunchPad) to significantly enhance their competitiveness and access global markets. Importantly, 50% of the SMEs will either be owned or led by women. Project is forecasted to create 11,000 new jobs by helping these SMEs generate higher revenues.

Focus will be on SMEs in the Export sector with a particular focus on the following sectors:

Agriculture / Agri-business exporters (tea, coffee, flowers, leather, etc).
Fishery and Aquaculture exporters
Travel &amp; Tourism sector (post-COVID-19 re-build efforts)</narrative>
  </description>
